<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wilfred the Hairy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 897</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Guifré el Pilós, Wilfred I of Barcelona · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-barcelona">House of Barcelona</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wilfred the Hairy was Count of Urgell and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerdanya">Cerdanya</a> from 870 and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girona">Girona</a> from 878, ruling most of the Catalan counties of the Spanish March. He resettled the depopulated plain of Vic and founded the monastery of Ripoll. He was the last count appointed by the Frankish king, and his sons inherited his counties, founding the dynasty of the counts of Barcelona.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wilfred-the-hairy.jpg" alt="Wilfred the Hairy" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rotlle-genealogic-guifre-I-de-barcelona.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the late ninth century <b>Wifred the Hairy</b>, count of Barcelona, Girona, Urgell and Cerdanya, made his counties hereditary in his family and founded the monastery of Ripoll, and his successors in Barcelona gradually gained precedence over the other counts.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Principality of Catalonia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 878 <b>Wilfred the Hairy</b> received it, and after his death in 897 his heirs inherited it without royal appointment.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-barcelona">County of Barcelona</a></li><li><blockquote>Besalú emerged as a county in the later 9th century, carved out of the lands of Girona and linked to the family of <b>Wilfred the Hairy</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-besalu">County of Besalú</a></li><li><blockquote>Sunifred, father of <b>Wilfred the Hairy</b>, held it in the 830s and 840s, and Wilfred himself became count in 870.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-cerdanya">County of Cerdanya</a></li><li><blockquote>From 878 Girona was held by <b>Wilfred the Hairy</b> with Barcelona and Osona.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-girona">County of Girona</a></li><li><blockquote>From about 879 <b>Wilfred the Hairy</b> repopulated the plain of Vic, restored its bishopric in 886 and founded the monasteries of Ripoll and Sant Joan de les Abadesses.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-osona">County of Osona</a></li></ul></section>
